window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>He knows what you want. That’s when the hunt begins.</b></p> <p>After barely surviving her first case in Grass Valley, FBI Special Agent Sadie Gray thought she’d seen the worst of humanity. She was wrong.</p> <p>Called to investigate a high-profile disappearance the FBI's San Francisco field office quietly passed over, Sadie and her handsome partner, Agent Brad Tulle, are thrust into a chilling new case—a mystery that stretches across state lines and defies logic. Leona Kolsch vanished without a trace… and the last confirmed sighting wasn’t in California. It was over 700 miles away—in Utah.</p> <p>As Sadie and Brad chase the trail, disturbing patterns emerge. Leona isn’t the only one. Three bodies. Two investigations. One signature.</p> <p>With mounting pressure and zero room for error, they uncover the terrifying truth: a calculating predator is targeting women across the West—someone who operates in silence, selects his victims with surgical precision… and always stays one step ahead.</p> <p>Tense, intelligent, and deeply atmospheric, <i>The Sight Unseen</i> is the second pulse-pounding novel in the Sadie Gray FBI series from <i>USA Today</i> bestselling authors R. B. Schow and Bailey James—perfect for fans of Karin Slaughter, Tess Gerritsen, Lisa Gardner, Mary Stone, and Alex Sigmore.</p> <p><b>BOOKS IN THIS ONGOING SERIES:</b></p> <ul> <li><i>The 34 In The Floor</i></li> <li><i>The Sight Unseen</i></li> <li><i>The Broken Girl</i></li> <li><i>The Murder Society</i></li> <li><i>The Girl With No Tomorrow</i></li> <li><i>The Place of Many Trees</i></li> <li><i>The Cold Quiet Everywhere</i> (<i>August, 2025</i>)</li> </ul> <p><b>Scroll up. Grab your copy now. Dive into your next binge-worthy listen!</b></p>"; 
